IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- LAYER 1: section 2028, "Consolidated block grants for Puerto Rico and American Samoa"
-- (7 U.S.C. 2028; lines 2731-2803 of usc07-ch51.txt, a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text).
-- Money is a NUMBER of dollars; a share or percentage is a fraction (20 percent is 0.20).
-- Every function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN or MAYBE NUMBER: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / JUST n is what the text says,
-- NOTHING is "not covered" (see NOTES.md, Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING).
-- A fiscal year is named by its number; the text does not define it, so a date is passed where a date is needed.

-- WHERE: Puerto Rico and American Samoa are in no value of the core's Area and in the core's Kind of place only as
-- "any other place", so section 2028 declares what it needs (NEEDS-CORE.md).
DECLARE `s 2028 place` IS ONE OF
    `s 2028 the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico`
    `s 2028 American Samoa`
    `s 2028 any other place`

-- s 2028(a)(2)(B)(ii): the three things the Commonwealth may spend the up-to-$6,000,000 on.
DECLARE `s 2028(a)(2)(B)(ii) cost` IS ONE OF
    `s 2028(a)(2)(B)(ii) upgrading and modernizing the electronic data processing system`
    `s 2028(a)(2)(B)(ii) implementing systems to simplify the determination of eligibility`
    `s 2028(a)(2)(B)(ii) operating systems to deliver the nutrition assistance through electronic benefit transfers`
    `s 2028(a)(2)(B)(ii) any other cost`

-- s 2028(d): the ways of taking the money that the penalty names.
DECLARE `s 2028(d) conduct` IS ONE OF
    `s 2028(d) embezzles`
    `s 2028(d) misapplies`
    `s 2028(d) steals`
    `s 2028(d) obtains by fraud`
    `s 2028(d) obtains by false statement`
    `s 2028(d) obtains by forgery`
    `s 2028(d) any other conduct`

§ `s 2028(a) Payments to governmental entities`

-- src:2733 | (1) Definition of governmental entity
-- src:2734 | In this subsection, the term “governmental entity” means—
-- src:2735 | (A) the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico; and
-- src:2736 | (B) American Samoa.
@ref s 2028(a)(1) governmental entity (src:2733-2736)
GIVEN place IS A `s 2028 place`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2028(a)(1) the place is a governmental entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `s 2028 the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2028 American Samoa` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the term governmental entity means"
    WHEN `s 2028 any other place` THEN JUST FALSE

-- The percentage is a fraction: 0.05 is 5 percent. "as adjusted by the percentage" is read as the amount TIMES (1 PLUS the percentage) (fork F-15 in NOTES.md).
-- src:2738 | (A) Amount of block grants
-- src:2739 | From the sums appropriated under this chapter, the Secretary shall, subject to this section, pay to governmental entities to pay the expenditures for nutrition assistance programs for needy persons as described in subparagraphs (B) and (C)—
-- src:2740 | (i) for fiscal year 2003, $1,401,000,000; and
-- src:2741 | (ii) subject to the availability of appropriations under section 2027(a) of this title, for each fiscal year thereafter, the amount specified in clause (i), as adjusted by the percentage by which the thrifty food plan has been adjusted under section 2012(u)(3) of this title between June 30, 2002, and June 30 of the immediately preceding fiscal year.
@ref s 2028(a)(2)(A) amount of block grants (src:2738-2741)
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      `s 2012(u)(3) the percentage by which the thrifty food plan was adjusted between the two dates` IS A NUMBER
      `s 2027(a) appropriations are available` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2028(a)(2)(A) the amount of the block grants for the fiscal year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `fiscal year` EQUALS 2003 THEN JUST 1_401_000_000
        IF `fiscal year` GREATER THAN 2003 THEN
            CONSIDER `s 2027(a) appropriations are available`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST (1_401_000_000 TIMES (1 PLUS `s 2012(u)(3) the percentage by which the thrifty food plan was adjusted between the two dates`))
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to the availability of appropriations under section 2027(a)"
            OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text gives an amount for fiscal year 2003 and each fiscal year thereafter
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2744 | For fiscal year 2003 and each fiscal year thereafter, the Secretary shall use 99.6 percent of the funds made available under subparagraph (A) for payment to the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico to pay—
-- src:2745 | (I) 100 percent of the expenditures by the Commonwealth for the fiscal year for the provision of nutrition assistance included in the plan of the Commonwealth approved under subsection (b); and
-- src:2746 | (II) 50 percent of the related administrative expenses.
@ref s 2028(a)(2)(B)(i) Commonwealth's share (src:2744-2746)
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      funds IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2028(a)(2)(B)(i) the Commonwealth's share of the funds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `fiscal year` AT LEAST 2003 THEN JUST (funds TIMES 0.996)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text speaks of fiscal year 2003 and each fiscal year thereafter
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 2028(a)(2)(B)(i)(I)-(II) 100 percent of expenditures and 50 percent of administrative expenses (src:2745-2746)
GIVEN `expenditures for nutrition assistance included in the approved plan` IS A NUMBER
      `related administrative expenses` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2028(a)(2)(B)(i) the payment toward the Commonwealth's expenditures and administrative expenses` MEANS
    (`expenditures for nutrition assistance included in the approved plan` TIMES 1) PLUS (`related administrative expenses` TIMES 0.5)

-- src:2748 | Notwithstanding clause (i), the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico may spend in fiscal year 2002 or 2003 not more than $6,000,000 of the amount required to be paid to the Commonwealth for fiscal year 2002 under this paragraph (as in effect on the day before May 13, 2002) to pay 100 percent of the costs of—
-- src:2749 | (I) upgrading and modernizing the electronic data processing system used to carry out nutrition assistance programs for needy persons;
-- src:2750 | (II) implementing systems to simplify the determination of eligibility to receive the nutrition assistance; and
-- src:2751 | (III) operating systems to deliver the nutrition assistance through electronic benefit transfers.
@ref s 2028(a)(2)(B)(ii) certain systems (src:2748-2751)
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      cost IS A `s 2028(a)(2)(B)(ii) cost`
      `total spent in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2028(a)(2)(B)(ii) the Commonwealth may spend the amount on the cost` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may spend in fiscal year 2002 or 2003"
        IF `fiscal year` EQUALS 2002 OR `fiscal year` EQUALS 2003 THEN
            CONSIDER cost
            WHEN `s 2028(a)(2)(B)(ii) any other cost` THEN NOTHING
            OTHERWISE
                BRANCH
                    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not more than $6,000,000"
                    IF `total spent in dollars` GREATER THAN 6_000_000 THEN JUST FALSE
                    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception is for "fiscal year 2002 or 2003"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2753 | For fiscal year 2003 and each fiscal year thereafter, the Secretary shall use 0.4 percent of the funds made available under subparagraph (A) for payment to American Samoa to pay 100 percent of the expenditures by American Samoa for a nutrition assistance program extended under section 1469d(c) of title 48.
@ref s 2028(a)(2)(C) American Samoa (src:2753)
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      funds IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2028(a)(2)(C) American Samoa's share of the funds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `fiscal year` AT LEAST 2003 THEN JUST (funds TIMES 0.004)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text speaks of fiscal year 2003 and each fiscal year thereafter
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 2028(a)(2)(C) 100 percent of the expenditures (src:2753)
GIVEN expenditures IS A NUMBER
      `the program is a nutrition assistance program extended under section 1469d(c) of title 48` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2028(a)(2)(C) the payment toward American Samoa's expenditures` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the program is a nutrition assistance program extended under section 1469d(c) of title 48` THEN JUST expenditures
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 1469d(c) of title 48 is not among the sources, and the payment is for "a nutrition assistance program extended under" it
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2755 | For fiscal year 2002 and each fiscal year thereafter, not more than 2 percent of the funds made available under this paragraph for the fiscal year to each governmental entity may be carried over to the following fiscal year.
@ref s 2028(a)(2)(D) carryover (src:2755)
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      funds IS A NUMBER
      `carried over` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2028(a)(2)(D) the carryover is within the limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text speaks of fiscal year 2002 and each fiscal year thereafter
        IF `fiscal year` LESS THAN 2002 THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not more than 2 percent of the funds"
        IF `carried over` GREATER THAN (funds TIMES 0.02) THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2757 | The Secretary shall, subject to the provisions of subsection (b), pay to the Commonwealth for the applicable fiscal year, at such times and in such manner as the Secretary may determine, the amount estimated by the Commonwealth pursuant to subsection (b)(1)(A)(iv), reduced or increased to the extent of any prior overpayment or current underpayment which the Secretary determines has been made under this section and with respect to which adjustment has not already been made under this subsection.
@ref s 2028(a)(3) time and manner of payments (src:2757)
GIVEN estimate IS A NUMBER
      `prior overpayment` IS A NUMBER
      `current underpayment` IS A NUMBER
      `s 2028(b)(1) the Commonwealth may receive payments` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2028(a)(3) the payment to the Commonwealth for the fiscal year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2028(b)(1) the Commonwealth may receive payments`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST ((estimate MINUS `prior overpayment`) PLUS `current underpayment`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to the provisions of subsection (b)"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2028(b) Plan for provision of assistance; approval; noncompliance`

-- src:2760 | (A) In order to receive payments under this chapter for any fiscal year, the Commonwealth shall have a plan for that fiscal year approved by the Secretary under this section. By July 1 of each year, if the Commonwealth wishes to receive payments, it shall submit a plan for the provision of the assistance described in subsection (a)(2)(B) for the following fiscal year which—
@ref s 2028(b)(1)(A) plan approved (src:2760)
GIVEN `the Commonwealth has a plan for the fiscal year approved by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2028(b)(1) the Commonwealth may receive payments` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Commonwealth has a plan for the fiscal year approved by the Secretary` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In order to receive payments under this chapter for any fiscal year, the Commonwealth shall have a plan for that fiscal year approved by the Secretary"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2760 | (A) In order to receive payments under this chapter for any fiscal year, the Commonwealth shall have a plan for that fiscal year approved by the Secretary under this section. By July 1 of each year, if the Commonwealth wishes to receive payments, it shall submit a plan for the provision of the assistance described in subsection (a)(2)(B) for the following fiscal year which—
@ref s 2028(b)(1)(A) by July 1 (src:2760)
GIVEN `the Commonwealth wishes to receive payments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date the plan is submitted` IS A DATE
      `year of submission` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2028(b)(1)(A) the plan is submitted in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the Commonwealth wishes to receive payments"
        IF (NOT `the Commonwealth wishes to receive payments`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `date the plan is submitted` AT MOST (Date 1 7 `year of submission`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "By July 1 of each year"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2761 | (i) designates the agency or agencies directly responsible for the administration, or supervision of the administration, of the program for the provision of such assistance;
-- src:2762 | (ii) assesses the food and nutrition needs of needy persons residing in the Commonwealth;
-- src:2763 | (iii) describes the program for the provision of such assistance, including the assistance to be provided and the persons to whom such assistance will be provided, and any agencies designated to provide such assistance, which program must meet such requirements as the Secretary may by regulation prescribe for the purpose of assuring that assistance is provided to the most needy persons in the jurisdiction;
-- src:2764 | (iv) estimates the amount of expenditures necessary for the provision of the assistance described in the program and related administrative expenses, up to the amount provided for payment by subsection (a)(2)(B); and
-- src:2765 | (v) includes such other information as the Secretary may require.
@ref s 2028(b)(1)(A)(i)-(v) contents of the plan (src:2761-2765)
GIVEN `designates the agency or agencies responsible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `assesses the food and nutrition needs of needy persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `describes the program and it meets the Secretary's requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `estimates the amount of expenditures in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount provided for payment by subsection (a)(2)(B) in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `includes the other information the Secretary requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2028(b)(1)(A) the plan has the required contents` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `designates the agency or agencies responsible`
            AND `assesses the food and nutrition needs of needy persons`
            AND `describes the program and it meets the Secretary's requirements`
            AND `estimates the amount of expenditures in dollars` AT MOST `the amount provided for payment by subsection (a)(2)(B) in dollars`
            AND `includes the other information the Secretary requires`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it shall submit a plan for the provision of the assistance described in subsection (a)(2)(B) for the following fiscal year which"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2767 | (i) The Secretary shall approve or disapprove any plan submitted pursuant to subparagraph (A) no later than August 1 of the year in which it is submitted. The Secretary shall approve any plan which complies with the requirements of subparagraph (A). If a plan is disapproved because it does not comply with any of the requirements of that paragraph the Secretary shall, except as provided in subparagraph (B)(ii), notify the appropriate agency in the Commonwealth that payments will not be made to it under subsection (a) for the fiscal year to which the plan applies until the Secretary is satisfied that there is no longer any such failure to comply, and until the Secretary is so satisfied, the Secretary will make no payments.
@ref s 2028(b)(1)(B)(i) August 1 (src:2767)
GIVEN `date the Secretary decides` IS A DATE
      `year of submission` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2028(b)(1)(B)(i) the Secretary's decision on the plan is in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `date the Secretary decides` AT MOST (Date 1 8 `year of submission`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no later than August 1 of the year in which it is submitted"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

@ref s 2028(b)(1)(B)(i) shall approve any plan which complies (src:2767)
GIVEN `the plan complies with the requirements of subparagraph (A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2028(b)(1)(B)(i) the Secretary shall approve the plan` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the plan complies with the requirements of subparagraph (A)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the Secretary shall do with a plan that complies and what follows a disapproval; it does not say whether a plan that does not comply may be approved
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 2028(b)(1)(B)(i) no payments until the Secretary is satisfied (src:2767)
GIVEN `the plan was disapproved because it does not comply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary is satisfied that there is no longer any failure to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has suspended the denial under clause (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2028(b)(1)(B)(i) payments may be made for the fiscal year of the plan` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except as provided in subparagraph (B)(ii)"
        IF `the Secretary has suspended the denial under clause (ii)` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "payments will not be made to it under subsection (a) for the fiscal year to which the plan applies until the Secretary is satisfied"
        IF `the plan was disapproved because it does not comply` AND (NOT `the Secretary is satisfied that there is no longer any failure to comply`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no disapproval, or the Secretary is now satisfied; the text does not itself say payments follow
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2768 | (ii) The Secretary may suspend the denial of payments under subparagraph (B)(i) for such period as the Secretary determines appropriate and instead withhold payments provided for under subsection (a), in whole or in part, for the fiscal year to which the plan applies, until the Secretary is satisfied that there is no longer any failure to comply with the requirements of subparagraph (A), at which time such withheld payments shall be paid.
@ref s 2028(b)(1)(B)(ii) suspend the denial (src:2768)
GIVEN `the Secretary has suspended the denial under clause (i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary is satisfied that there is no longer any failure to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2028(b)(1)(B)(ii) the withheld payments are to be paid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary has suspended the denial under clause (i)` AND `the Secretary is satisfied that there is no longer any failure to comply` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "withhold payments provided for under subsection (a), in whole or in part, for the fiscal year to which the plan applies, until the Secretary is satisfied"
        IF `the Secretary has suspended the denial under clause (i)` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): clause (ii) applies only where the Secretary has suspended the denial of payments
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2028(b)(2) Audit, report and noncompliance`

-- src:2770 | (A) The Commonwealth shall provide for a biennial audit of expenditures under its program for the provision of the assistance described in subsection (a)(2)(B), and within 120 days of the end of each fiscal year in which the audit is made, shall report to the Secretary the findings of such audit.
@ref s 2028(b)(2)(A) biennial audit and 120 days (src:2770)
GIVEN `end of the fiscal year in which the audit is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2028(b)(2)(A) the last day for the report of the audit findings` MEANS
    `end of the fiscal year in which the audit is made` PLUS 120

@ref s 2028(b)(2)(A) within 120 days of the end of each fiscal year in which the audit is made (src:2770)
GIVEN `end of the fiscal year in which the audit is made` IS A DATE
      `date the findings are reported` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2028(b)(2)(A) the report of the audit findings is in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `date the findings are reported` AT MOST (`s 2028(b)(2)(A) the last day for the report of the audit findings` `end of the fiscal year in which the audit is made`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 120 days of the end of each fiscal year in which the audit is made"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- "biennial" is read as once every two years (fork F-1 in NOTES.md); the fiscal years are passed as numbers.
@ref s 2028(b)(2)(A) biennial audit (src:2770)
GIVEN `fiscal year of the last audit` IS A NUMBER
      `fiscal year of this audit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2028(b)(2)(A) the audit is biennial` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `fiscal year of this audit` MINUS `fiscal year of the last audit` AT MOST 2 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commonwealth shall provide for a biennial audit of expenditures"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2771 | (B) Within 120 days of the end of the fiscal year, the Commonwealth shall provide the Secretary with a statement as to whether the payments received under subsection (a) for that fiscal year exceeded the expenditures by it during that year for which payment is authorized under this section, and if so, by how much, and such other information as the Secretary may require.
@ref s 2028(b)(2)(B) statement within 120 days (src:2771)
GIVEN `end of the fiscal year` IS A DATE
      `date the statement is provided` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2028(b)(2)(B) the statement is provided in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `date the statement is provided` AT MOST (`end of the fiscal year` PLUS 120) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 120 days of the end of the fiscal year, the Commonwealth shall provide the Secretary with a statement"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

@ref s 2028(b)(2)(B) contents of the statement (src:2771)
GIVEN `states whether the payments exceeded the expenditures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `payments exceeded the expenditures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `states by how much` IS A BOOLEAN
      `gives the other information the Secretary requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2028(b)(2)(B) the statement has the required contents` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `states whether the payments exceeded the expenditures`
            AND ((NOT `payments exceeded the expenditures`) OR `states by how much`)
            AND `gives the other information the Secretary requires`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a statement as to whether the payments received under subsection (a) for that fiscal year exceeded the expenditures"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2773 | (i) If the Secretary finds that there is a substantial failure by the Commonwealth to comply with any of the requirements of subparagraphs (A) and (B), or to comply with the requirements of subsection (b)(1)(A) in the administration of a plan approved under subsection (b)(1)(B), the Secretary shall, except as provided in subparagraph (C)(ii), notify the appropriate agency in the Commonwealth that further payments will not be made to it under subsection (a) until the Secretary is satisfied that there will no longer be any such failure to comply, and until the Secretary is so satisfied, the Secretary shall make no further payments.
@ref s 2028(b)(2)(C)(i) no further payments (src:2773)
GIVEN `the Secretary finds a substantial failure to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary is satisfied that there will no longer be any such failure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has suspended the termination under clause (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2028(b)(2)(C)(i) further payments may be made` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except as provided in subparagraph (C)(ii)"
        IF `the Secretary has suspended the termination under clause (ii)` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "further payments will not be made to it under subsection (a) until the Secretary is satisfied that there will no longer be any such failure to comply"
        IF `the Secretary finds a substantial failure to comply` AND (NOT `the Secretary is satisfied that there will no longer be any such failure`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no finding, or the Secretary is now satisfied; the text does not itself say payments follow
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2774 | (ii) The Secretary may suspend the termination of payments under subparagraph (C)(i) for such period as the Secretary determines appropriate, and instead withhold payments provided for under subsection (a), in whole or in part, until the Secretary is satisfied that there will no longer be any failure to comply with the requirements of subparagraphs (A) and (B) and subsection (b)(1)(A), at which time such withheld payments shall be paid.
@ref s 2028(b)(2)(C)(ii) suspend the termination (src:2774)
GIVEN `the Secretary has suspended the termination under clause (i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary is satisfied that there will no longer be any failure to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2028(b)(2)(C)(ii) the withheld payments are to be paid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary has suspended the termination under clause (i)` AND `the Secretary is satisfied that there will no longer be any failure to comply` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "withhold payments provided for under subsection (a), in whole or in part, until the Secretary is satisfied"
        IF `the Secretary has suspended the termination under clause (i)` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): clause (ii) applies only where the Secretary has suspended the termination of payments
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2775 | (iii) Upon a finding under subparagraph (C)(i) of a substantial failure to comply with any of the requirements of subparagraphs (A) and (B) and subsection (b)(1)(A), the Secretary may, in addition to or in lieu of any action taken under subparagraphs (C)(i) and (C)(ii), refer the matter to the Attorney General with a request that injunctive relief be sought to require compliance by the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico, and upon suit by the Attorney General in an appropriate district court of the United States and a showing that noncompliance has occurred, appropriate injunctive relief shall issue.
@ref s 2028(b)(2)(C)(iii) referral to the Attorney General (src:2775)
